Content licence for content/lessons/ (PROVISIONAL)
==================================================

Status: provisional. These are the terms the R2 plan proceeds on (docs/phase-3.md, "Your part": "The content licence:
lesson text CC BY 4.0, patches and codes CC0, code MIT"; docs/learn.md, "Packs"). The owner has not confirmed them yet,
and confirms or changes them before lane C1 writes the first real pack. Until then, contribute on these terms or do not
contribute to this directory.

What is under which licence
---------------------------

  * Lesson text (the markdown steps, titles, objectives and every other prose field of a pack):
    Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International (CC BY 4.0).
    https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/legalcode

  * Patches, factory presets, challenge codes and every other piece of machine-readable data in a pack
    (patches/*.patch.json, the targets and codes a lesson names):
    Creative Commons Zero 1.0 Universal (CC0 1.0), a public-domain dedication.
    https://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/legalcode

  * Code (the lesson player in crates/enth-learn, the xtask commands, the tests): MIT, as the rest of the repository.
    See the LICENSE file at the repository root. Nothing under content/lessons/ is code.

Contributing
------------

By contributing to content/lessons/ you agree that your text is licensed CC BY 4.0 and your patches and codes CC0 1.0,
and that you wrote them or may license them so. Do not copy lesson text, patches or presets from a source whose licence
does not allow this (a synth manual, a preset pack, another project's lessons), and do not use GPL, LGPL or AGPL
material: AGENTS.md's licensing rules apply to content as they do to code.

Every pack carries a CREDITS.md that names its authors and repeats these terms, and its manifest records them as
`license.text = "CC-BY-4.0"` and `license.patches = "CC0-1.0"`; `cargo xtask lesson-check` enforces those ids.

This file is not legal advice and does not replace the full licence texts at the links above.
